{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And I will lead you upright (קוממיות).</b> I have already mentioned above that this parashah, with its wondrous promises, was never fulfilled in the two Temples, but will be fulfilled in the future. And from this verse our Rabbis of blessed memory proved that the statures will return in the future to two hundred cubits — this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in tractate Sanhedrin and likewise in the chapter HaSefinah: ״קוממיות״ — two statures of Adam the first, the words of Rabbi Meir; Rabbi Yehudah says: one hundred cubits, like the stature of the Hekhal, as it is said (ibid. 144) ״מחוטבות תבנית היכל״. And what is said there, that the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to bring precious stones and pearls and engrave in them ten by twenty in height and set them in the gates of Jerusalem, as it is said (Isaiah 54) ״ושעריך לאבני אקדח״ — from which it would appear that the statures will be twenty cubits, no more — they therefore needed to say that this is not said concerning the gates of houses, for how would those statures enter through them, but rather concerning the gates of the windows." "<b>Here,</b> this parashah of these good promises began with alef — ״אם בחקותי״ — and ended with tav — ״קוממיות״ — and this is to indicate that these blessings come to Israel in full only at a time when they have fulfilled the entire Torah from alef to tav. And the parashah of the curses adjacent to it begins with vav — ״ואם לא תשמעו לי״ — and the entire parashah ends with heh — ״בהר סיני ביד משה״ — and this is half of the Name, after what is written (Psalms 91:15) ״עמו אנכי בצרה״." "<b>And know</b> that the verses of the curses are more numerous than the verses of the blessings, and likewise with the curses in Deuteronomy (Mishneh Torah). And this was in order to threaten the creatures and frighten them away from transgression by the multiplicity of the curses. And thus we find regarding the Shekhinah, which is the attribute of justice, that it was ״כאש אוכלת בראש ההר לעיני בני ישראל״ (Exodus 24), while the mercy was within it. And this is the secret of the verse (Psalms 45) ״כל כבודה בת מלך פנימה״ — he explains that the attribute called ״כל״, which is the attribute of ״כבודה״, that is, the attribute of glory — ״בת מלך״ — is from within, even though it is clothed on the outside in settings of gold." "<b>And they said</b> in the Midrash: Do not say that when He came to bless, He diminished the blessings, and when He came to curse, He multiplied the curses. Rather, in the blessings He begins with alef and ends with tav — letters that are far apart from one another, to hint that the blessings have a root; but in the curses He begins with vav and ends with heh, to hint that they go backward, for they have no root — for from vav to heh is nothing."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:48.721137986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}